Subject: [PATCH 0003] Avoid full vector copies when counting serialized bytes

The `countBytes` helper takes each vector by value. Every serialization call
therefore copies one complete SPZ attribute vector only to read its size.
Large assets incur avoidable allocation, memory use, and copy time.

Pass the vector by const reference. This change does not alter the wire format.

Upstream status: not submitted.

Applies to: nianticlabs/spz @ 2cf0be04d86b5f9632d9073ccbbe3b1e6a609f31 (v2.1.0)

--- a/src/cc/load-spz.cc
+++ b/src/cc/load-spz.cc
@@ -99,4 +99,4 @@ float invSigmoid(float x) {
 template <typename T>
-size_t countBytes(std::vector<T> vec) {
+size_t countBytes(const std::vector<T>& vec) {
   return vec.size() * sizeof(vec[0]);
 }
